rg/entity/Q79","http://viaf.org/viaf/242059233","http://viaf.org/viaf/125499078","https://d-nb.info/gnd/4000556-2","http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n80061791","http://data.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cb11863530z","http://data.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cb15238583n","http://data.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cb11938556d","http://www.idref.fr/027316866/id","http://www.idref.fr/026375680/id","http://id.ndl.go.jp/auth/ndlna/00562068","http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D004534","https://www.freebase.com/m/02k54","https://g.co/kg/m/02k54","http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/Z01.058.266.317","http://datos.bne.es/resource/XX450764","https://livedata.bibsys.no/authority/90074621","https://sws.geonames.org/357994/","http://vocab.getty.edu/tgn/7016833","http://id.worldcat.org/fast/1208755","http://www.yso.fi/onto/yso/p105841","http://babelnet.org/rdf/s00005255n","http://nomisma.org/id/egypt","http://zbw.eu/stw/descriptor/17745-0","http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept706","http://www.yso.fi/onto/ysa/Y105841","http://dbpedia.org/resource/Egypt"]}],"providedCHOs":[{"about":"/item/2021606/resource_document_rijksmuseum_van_oudheden_AMM16i"}],"proxies":[{"about":"/proxy/europeana/2021606/resource_document_rijksmuseum_van_oudheden_AMM16i","dcCoverage":{"def":["http://data.europeana.eu/place/32"]},"dcIdentifier":{"def":["http://data.collectienederland.nl/resource/document/rijksmuseum-van-oudheden/AMM16i"]},"proxyIn":["/aggregation/europeana/2021606/resource_document_rijksmuseum_van_oudheden_AMM16i"],"proxyFor":"/item/2021606/resource_document_rijksmuseum_van_oudheden_AMM16i","lineage":["/proxy/provider/2021606/resource_document_rijksmuseum_van_oudheden_AMM16i"],"edmType":"IMAGE","europeanaProxy":true},{"about":"/proxy/provider/2021606/resource_document_rijksmuseum_van_oudheden_AMM16i","dcCoverage":{"def":["Egypte"]},"dcDate":{"def":["Grieks-Romeinse Periode; Romeinse keizertijd 30 v.Chr.-640 n.Chr."]},"dcDescription":{"def":["krokodil The central area of the animal's back has been covered with a gridded pattern of thin strips of doubled linen (medium-fine warp-faced tabby weave, about 14 x 36 threads/cm2). The extant remains comprise four longitudinal overlapping strips along the sides and seven over the spine; the areas in between once had a fill of dark brown linen, of which only remains are still visible. Of the transverse elements there are only two strips of natural linen over the foremost part of the back; both show that originally there was a broader strip of dark brown linen under this, and there must have been more of these transverse bands, now completely lost. The corresponding area of the ventral side has lost its outer sheet by decay and merely shows various diagonal bandages which have much darkened by decay. The head is wrapped in dark brown cloth, fixed by means of a concentric band of natural linen around the neck (doubled, width 0.5 cm) and by several windings of yarn. The eyes have been modelled; it cannot be assessed whether any appliques were once present. The tail is straight; the whole rear end has been wrapped in concentric bandages of rather coarse natural linen (about 9 x 24 threads/cm2), with traces of at least two transverse straps of dark brown cloth."]},"dcIdentifier":{"def":["AMM 16i"]},"dcRights":{"def":["Creative Commons By-licensie: bron: Rijksmuseum van Oudheden, Leiden"]},"dcSubject":{"def":["krokodil"]},"dcTitle":{"def":["mummie ; reptiel ; krokodil ; dierenmummie"]},"dcType":{"def":["mummie ; reptiel ; krokodil ; dierenmummie"]},"dctermsCreated":{"def":["Grieks-Romeinse Periode; Romeinse keizertijd 30 v.Chr.-640 n.Chr."]},"dctermsExtent":{"def":["36,7 x 7,3 x 4,8 cm"]},"dctermsIsReferencedBy":{"def":["Leemans, Description raisonnée (1840) N 31 Boeser, Catalogus (1907) E.XLV.26 M.J. Raven/W.K. Taconis, Egyptian mummies (Turnhout 2005), cat. 116 A. Quertinmont (red.), Du Nil à Alexandrie (Morlanwelz 2013), cat. 45"]},"dctermsMedium":{"def":["organisch ; mummie (dierlijk) ; linnen"]},"proxyIn":["/aggregation/provider/2021606/resource_docume